3. Restrictions on sale and paid hosting

Without a separate written license from the relevant copyright holders,
You must not:

(a) sell, rent, sublicense for a fee, or otherwise provide copies of the
Software or Modified Versions in exchange for monetary or other commercial
consideration; or
(b) provide the Software or Modified Versions to third parties as a paid
hosted, managed, cloud, or software-as-a-service offering, whether running
on Your infrastructure or infrastructure operated for a customer.

These restrictions apply to source and binary distributions, renamed or
rebranded versions, and offerings bundled with another product or service.
A subscription, membership, bundle fee, or other indirect payment that is
required to obtain the Software or access its functionality counts as payment.
Free redistribution must preserve these restrictions for recipients.
An organization's internal use under section 2 is not paid hosting merely
because the organization pays its employees or contractors or purchases
general-purpose infrastructure for its own use. Fees solely for advice or
support are permitted only when they do not include a Software sale or a
paid hosted or managed offering prohibited above.

